From 848df5196813c864c089eda9b6359bc29ee910df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:46:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/42] nas-relay: serve QMX serial port 3 to PC software on
 TCP 7356

With the QMX set to "USB serial ports" = 3, the relay now serves the
radio's third serial port as a plain TCP serial port (default 7356,
--serial-port N, 0 = off), so PC software (WSJT-X CAT, rigctld, logging
programs, a terminal) can control the radio alongside the Tab5.

- Generic handling of the QMX's extra serial ports (port 2 = Tab5
  Radio menus, port 3 = PC); clear messages when the radio has too few.
- Shared radio manager: the QMX is opened by the first user (Tab5 or
  PC) and released by the last; either can come and go independently.
- --probe reports the number of serial ports; --fake emulates 3 ports.
- README / docker-compose updated; documentation PDF regenerated.

Firmware unchanged (QMXR/1 protocol unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
